SUMMARY:Bent Creek Wolf Knob Loop - 8.5 Miles\, 1600 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nBack to Bent Creek. This loop star
 ts at Rice Pinnacle parking lot\, goes up to Wolf Knob and then loops arou
 nd and back down Boyd Branch. This loop has some easier fire road trails a
 long with one steep climb up and down. Some of these trails are mountain b
 ike trails although we don't tend to see many on a Monday morning.\n\nThis
  is a hard hike. Expect rocky\, rooty trail\, steep climbs\, and steep up 
 and downhills. In fall\, leaves can hide rocks and roots and make footing 
 slippery. We will keep a moderate pace when possible (last time we had a m
 oving avg of 2.8 mph). Please only sign up if you're comfortable with stee
 p\, uneven terrain and hiking 8.5 miles. If you're not sure\, message me f
 irst and I'm happy to talk it through.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explor
 e/custom-routes/rice-pinnacle-parking-to-wolf-knob-to-boyd-branch-2f0b4c5\
 n\n**CARPOOL**\nI don't think a carpool is necessary for this one but feel
  free to arrange something via event chat or comments.\n\n**WEATHER**\nThe
  weather currently might be okay for Monday but I'll watch the weather and
  post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if there is a chance of severe wea
 ther or lightning during this time period..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can mes
 sage me through MeetUp or phone until the hike starts although cell recept
 ion may be sketchy\, (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hikin
 g Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from 
 the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and aff
 irm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipm
 ent\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neit
 her your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety 
 nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any i
 njuries\, damages\, or losses.
